# Treacherous Greed is an instant, and "dealt damage" is any damage, not only combat damage. On Bot2's turn 4, with Bot2's Bear Cub
# on the stack, Bot1 pings Bot2 with Prodigal Sorcerer (19), then casts Greed: Bot1's own Bear Cub has dealt no damage this turn and
# is refused as the sacrifice, Prodigal Sorcerer (tapped for its ability, damage dealt) is accepted. Bot1 draws three (the hand goes 0 -> 3)
# and gains 3 (23); Bot2 loses 3 (16). Bot2's Cub resolves afterwards.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Prodigal Sorcerer
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Treacherous Greed
Bear Cub
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Bear Cub
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Prodigal Sorcerer.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bear Cub.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Bear Cub.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Prodigal Sorcerer.Activate(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Treacherous Greed.Cast
! Bot1.Choose(Bear Cub)
Bot1.Choose(Prodigal Sorcerer)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Treacherous Greed; Prodigal Sorcerer
Bot1.Battlefield.Bear Cub.Power = 2
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Life = 23
Bot2.Life = 16
